    "narrative": "For our June 26th slate, **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) anchor our offensive production, serving as our strongest plays. **James Wood** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a high-probability base-stealing environment against a slow-delivering opposing catcher, while **Mickey Moniak** is poised for a breakout performance in the two-hole, buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) against the starter. **Corbin Carroll** (74.38) and **Jose Caballero** (71.07) follow closely behind; despite both facing pitchers who are elite at holding runners, their projected volume and efficiency ensure they remain essential components of our pursuit for stolen base categories.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Alex Freeland**, who posted a respectable 47.22 but lacked the necessary ceiling to displace our starters in a crowded middle infield. Ultimately, our optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency and order-slot advantages of **Brice Turang** and **Max Muncy**. We are keeping a close watch on **Jose Caballero**, whose high-value matchup is shadowed by a 35% rain risk; should a washout occur, we are prepared to pivot. Additionally, while **Austin Riley** remains a lock in the lineup, we are monitoring his status closely, as his projected output is contingent on wind conditions that currently favor his power profile. We continue to hold **Trevor Story** on the IL, while bench options like **Seiya Suzuki** were bypassed due to a tough matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA starter, keeping our daily efficiency metrics prioritized over pure name value.",
